<h1>Supplier onboarding</h1>

<p>Before a new supplier can be added to our approved panel and receive a first purchase order, our procurement team needs the following, in addition to a completed credit application:</p>

<ul class="list">
    <li>Company registration details and registered address</li>
    <li>Bank account details for payment on our standard sixty-day terms</li>
    <li>Current public liability and, where relevant, product liability insurance certificates</li>
    <li>Copies of any relevant quality certificates, such as ISO 9001 or an industry-specific equivalent</li>
    <li>A signed acknowledgement of our <a href="/suppliers/terms">terms of supply</a></li>
</ul>

<p>Once these are received, a member of our procurement team will confirm the supplier's inclusion on the approved panel and issue portal access for order tracking and certificate submission. Onboarding typically takes between one and three weeks depending on the process being approved.</p>

<p>Questions about onboarding should be sent through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Existing suppliers with an active account should use <a href="/signin">sign in</a> instead.</p>
